From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: bind Direct Switch to the QSDK NSS/PPE stack

The PPE side (qca-nss-ppe + qca-nss-dp) owns the Direct Switch rings, so
ath12k no longer needs its own kernel transport.  Replace the qcom_ppe_ds_*
calls with the exported ppe_ds_wlan_* API and hand the ring callback set over
as ppe_ds_wlan_ops.

- nss/: verbatim copies of the public nss-ppe headers, so the ABI cannot drift
- ppe_ds.c: node id -> ds lookup for the callbacks, ppe_ds_wlan_* for
  instance handling, ppe_vp_alloc()/ppe_vp_cfg_update() for VP routing
- allow IPQ5332: the rings are host memory on the WMAC side and the PPE side
  drives them, so the QCN9274-only gate is no longer meaningful
- ath-qualcommbe.mk: kmod-ath12k depends on kmod-qca-nss-ppe-ds/-vp

